From: E2B kernel build <kernel-build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tools/libbpf: preserve const when splitting a search path

New glibc headers expose a const-preserving strchr() when _GNU_SOURCE enables
C23 interfaces, including when the compiler uses an older language dialect.
next_path is only used for a pointer difference; it never modifies the string.
Preserve the const qualification to build the 6.1 host tools with these headers.

diff --git a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
--- a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
@@ -10748,7 +10748,7 @@ static int resolve_full_path(const char *file, char *result, size_t result_sz)
 		if (!search_paths[i])
 			continue;
 		for (s = search_paths[i]; s != NULL; s = strchr(s, ':')) {
-			char *next_path;
+			const char *next_path;
 			int seg_len;
 
 			if (s[0] == ':')
